<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbek Jan-May trade gap widens to $274.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Uzbek Jan-May trade gap widens to $274.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan posted a trade deficit of $274.7 million in the first five months of this year after a $19.2 million surplus in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>			UZBEK MERCHANDISE TRADE</p>
<p>    (million dollars)		   Jan-May 97   Jan-May 96</p>
<p>    Exports			 1,553.2     1,384.3</p>
<p>    Imports			 1,827.9     1,365.1</p>
<p>    Trade balance		  -274.7	 +19.2</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
